WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.000
[Electronic music]
How Bluelines works
From a click on any page to a fixed bug.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.600
Step 1: Open any website.
Bluelines adds a small dock to every page. No account, nothing to set up.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:12.600
Step 2: Turn on Inspect.
Click Inspect in the dock, or press Alt + Shift + M.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:18.600
Step 3: Hover any element.
Its selector and size show up as you move.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.600
Step 4: Click it to add a note.
The note box opens right next to the element.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:26.600
Step 5: Pick a category.
Every install starts with one: UI.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:31.600
Step 6: Write what should change.
The selector, size and a screenshot are saved with it.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.600
Step 7: Send it to your AI agent.
Optional. Pick the agent before you save.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.600
Step 8: Press Enter to save.
Shift + Enter adds a new line instead. (Enter)

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:45.600
Step 9: Make your own categories.
Type any word in the category menu.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:50.600
Step 10: Open the sidebar.
Every note on the page, with numbered pins. (Alt + Shift + D)

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:54.600
Step 11: Filter by status.
Open, sent to an agent, needs a re-pin, or done.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.600
Step 12: Copy in their format.
Markdown, JSON, XML, Notion, Linear, Jira, Slack, GitHub.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:03.100
Step 13: See it all in a table.
This page, or every page you have marked.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:07.600
Step 14: Export it.
Excel with screenshots, PDF, HTML, CSV, Markdown, JSON or ZIP.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:13.600
Step 15: Connect your AI agent.
Settings → Connect to AI agents. Works over MCP.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:19.600
Step 16: Your agent fixes it.
It reads the note, changes the code, replies and resolves.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:26.000
Bluelines
See. Mark. Explain. Ship.
Full guide · getbluelines.netlify.app/docs
